    {
      "id": 177930,
      "name": "robb8888",
      "username": "robb8888",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2016-06-24T03:05:31.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Mint, but it was kind of a boring, no-fun slog. &nbsp;Just about every turn, there was some sort of environment/Deadline effect that did 2-3 damage to *every* target on the board, which wiped out constructs and 'bots almost as soon as I could get them out. &nbsp;Plus, some of these heroes' best combos/tricks (Salvage Yard, Robot Reclamation, Omni-U's base power, Unflagging Animation) depend on them getting stuff out of their trash, and the %#$@^#% &nbsp;Severed Ley-Line meant that their trash kept getting recycled into their decks. &nbsp;</p><p>By Round 3-4, I could tell I was going to win by Fixer just relentlessly pounding on Deadline, and the rest of the heroes chipping in little bits whenever they could keep their best bots/constructs/components out for more than a round or two. &nbsp; Winning isn't much fun when 3/4 of your heroes never really get any of their good combos going. &nbsp;The thought of the wet \"crack/gush\" sound as Fixer took Deadline out by burying a crowbar in his skull kinda made up for it, though.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/5/56bd8ae81ccd72059dad3827b96db5997e698138.png\" alt=\"image_5.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"cnl9EbuLZ0w0fw0VhX3gi7zYSCY\" width=\"320\" height=\"240\"></p>",
      "post_number": 12,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-20T18:36:10.682Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
