      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Mint, but it was kind of a boring, no-fun slog. &nbsp;Just about every turn, there was some sort of environment/Deadline effect that did 2-3 damage to *every* target on the board, which wiped out constructs and &#39;bots almost as soon as I could get them out. &nbsp;Plus, some of these heroes&#39; best combos/tricks (Salvage Yard, Robot Reclamation, Omni-U&#39;s base power, Unflagging Animation) depend on them getting stuff out of their trash, and the %#$@^#% &nbsp;Severed Ley-Line meant that their trash kept getting recycled into their decks. &nbsp;</p><p>By Round 3-4, I could tell I was going to win by Fixer just relentlessly pounding on Deadline, and the rest of the heroes chipping in little bits whenever they could keep their best bots/constructs/components out for more than a round or two. &nbsp; Winning isn&#39;t much fun when 3/4 of your heroes never really get any of their good combos going. &nbsp;The thought of the wet &quot;crack/gush&quot; sound as Fixer took Deadline out by burying a crowbar in his skull kinda made up for it, though.&nbsp;</p>\n\n![image_5.png|320x240](upload://cnl9EbuLZ0w0fw0VhX3gi7zYSCY.png)",
